---
import FeatureCard from '@chassis-ui/docs/components/FeatureCard.astro'
---

<section class="home-section py-3xl md:py-6xl">
  <div class="container 2xl section-content py-3xl md:py-6xl">
    <div class="row mb-3xl md:mb-6xl">
      <div class="section-header col lg:col-10 xl:col-8 text-center mx-auto">
        <h2 class="section-title font-3xl md:font-4xl lg:font-5xl mb-xs md:mb-sm lg:mb-md">
          <span class="font-normal d-block">Built for</span> Production at Scale
        </h2>
        <p class="section-body md:font-lg lg:font-xl m-0">
          A build for products with several brands, apps and platforms. It takes the files from the
          export of the design tool to the folder an app reads.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-features row row-cols-1 md:row-cols-2 g-md md:g-xl">
      <div class="col">
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-swatchbook">
          <Fragment slot="title">Multi-Brand Architecture</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            The folders of the source are the brands: default/ for the files every brand gets, and a
            folder per brand for its overrides. The build lays the brand over the default files.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-laptop-mobile">
          <Fragment slot="title">Platform-Specific Names</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Applies the naming of each platform: kebab-case for the web, snake_case for iOS and
            Android, and the ic_ prefix for Android icons. Subfolders are kept on every platform.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-layer-group">
          <Fragment slot="title">Resolution Variant Handling</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Reads the @2x and @3x indicator of a file name. The web and iOS keep it in the name, and
            Android gets the file in its density folder, such as drawable-xhdpi.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-filter">
          <Fragment slot="title">Format Filtering by Platform</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            The web gets WOFF and WOFF2 fonts with their stylesheets, iOS and Android get TTF and
            OTF. WebP images go to the web and Android, and each platform gets the icon formats it
            can use.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-zap">
          <Fragment slot="title">CLI Build Filters</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            The --brand, --app and --platform options build a part of the output and keep the rest.
            A CI job builds the one job its app reads.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-shield-check">
          <Fragment slot="title">Checks</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            A validator compares the output with the source, a contract check names the files a
            consumer reads, a source lint checks the names, and an analyzer reports sizes and files
            with the same content.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
